Gizmo Fizzcrank marched into Stranglethorn with his Succubus, Lilis, confident her lashes would melt trolls faster than any blueberry could.  
First raptor pack: Lilis ripped one apart, but two friends charged Gizmo. He tried to Seduce—spell pushback, broken cast, claws in his face, graveyard run.  
Second attempt: he pre-Seduced a caster, dotted it, pulled a patrol—Seduction dr’d, Lilis couldn’t peel, another corpse run.  
By the third tiger, Gizmo sighed, summoned the Voidwalker, let it Torment everything while he rained fire from behind its big purple back.  
No bandages, no downtime, no death.  
He never looked back.

Answer: the Voidwalker’s taunt and shield let the Warlock chain-pull mobs with zero risk or downtime; the Succubus deals more damage but can’t save the squishy caster when things go sideways, so the safer, self-healing tank pet wins the leveling day. [end of text]


